  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "",
    "plain": "Can the **flypitch** project (Han & Van Doorn, 2020), which formally verified the independence of the Continuum Hypothesis in Lean 3 via Cohen forcing, be ported to Lean 4 and then extended to class-sized partial orders so that it can prove Easton's theorem on the values of the continuum function $\\kappa \\mapsto 2^\\kappa$ for regular cardinals $\\kappa$?",
    "whyMatters": []
  },
